// Fixture of the transport tests (idlc/tests/transport.rs): one method
// that carries both bytes and a capability, so a request and a reply can
// exceed the limits while holding a capability.

/// Holds a frame next to some data, used only to test the transport.
///
/// Revocation of the caller's endpoint capability mid-call ends the call with
/// `revoked`; a provider restart ends it with `peer_gone`; cancellation ends it
/// with `cancelled`. In each case there is no reply data, and the method is
/// safe to retry.
protocol hold.Holder version 1 {
    /// Takes `frame` and `data`; returns a frame and data of the provider's
    /// choice.
    put @1 (data: bytes, frame: cap<Frame>) -> (data: bytes, frame: cap<Frame>);
}
